Subject: Reduce-BlockState-Memory-Usage

Author: VeltisMC Development Team
Date: 2026-06-19

Reason:
Vanilla BlockState storage uses full BlockState objects for every
block in every loaded chunk. With chunk sections containing up to
4096 blocks and worlds having thousands of chunks, this consumes
significant heap memory. Moonrise's fast_palette optimizations reduce
the memory footprint of block state palettes using more compact
representations.

Impact:
Reduced heap usage per chunk. Servers can maintain more loaded chunks
within the same memory budget, improving player experience in
exploration-heavy gameplay.

Migration Note:
This patch activates Moonrise's palette optimizations. The block
counting system also reduces overhead from tracking block counts
per chunk section.
